{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790621972943,"sessionID":"ses_f169d4360ffe2MwsyHYqQbxQeg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_b63ddf0b48c44bddbb07d11c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"agentgraph --help","description":"Check agentgraph CLI availability"},"output":"Agent-native code understanding: symbol graph, call graph, impact analysis\n\nUsage: agentgraph.exe [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>\n\nCommands:\n  index         Build or refresh the local index (incremental by content hash). Multi-root: `index --workspace <manifest.json>` or repeated `--workspace-root <dir>`\n  workspace     Workspace multi-root commands (single SQLite store + root_id)\n  stats         Show index statistics\n  find          Find symbol definitions by exact name (falls back to fuzzy on no match)\n  callers       List call sites / references of a symbol\n  blast-radius  High-level blast-radius recipe: auto sound vs default window + honesty payload\n  who-calls     High-level who-calls recipe: implementors separated by default; --noisy merges\n  impact        Blast radius: who transitively depends on this symbol\n  related       Files most related to a symbol (for retrieval scoping)\n  importers     Files that import a given file (module-level edges)\n  enrich        Optional LLM pass: one-line responsibility descriptions for symbols\n  watch         Poll and reindex when source files change\n  subset        Scan the index for language-subset S violations (L2)\n  diff          Compare indexed edge set against the snapshot baseline written at `index` time\n  export        Export index as SCIP protobuf binary (official scip CLI) or LSIF JSONL\n  mcp           Run as an MCP server over stdio\n  bench-query   Measure callers/impact latency percentiles in-process (PLAN query SLO)\n  macro         Optional macro-expanded sidecar commands (CLI default OFF)\n  graph         Render a local self-contained HTML code-graph around a symbol\n  help          Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)\n\nOptions:\n      --root <ROOT>\n          Project root to index (defaults to cwd)\n      --workspace <WORKSPACE>\n          Workspace manifest JSON: `{ \"roots\": [{\"id\",\"path\"},…] }` or array of paths. Shared store defaults to `<manifest_dir>/.agentgraph/index.db`\n      --workspace-root <WORKSPACE_ROOT>\n          Workspace project root (repeatable). On `index`: roots to ingest. On queries: filter rows to that `root_id`\n      --workspace-db <WORKSPACE_DB>\n          Explicit shared workspace SQLite path (overrides manifest/first-root defaults)\n      --workspace-alias <PKG=ROOT>\n          Workspace package-name alias (repeatable): `--workspace-alias <pkg>=<root_id>` or `--workspace-alias <pkg>=<path>`. Example: `--workspace-alias @demo/registry=registry`. Partial package map for cross-root imports — **not** full TypeScript resolution\n  -h, --help\n          Print help\n  -V, --version\n          Print version\n","metadata":{"output":"Agent-native code understanding: symbol graph, call graph, impact analysis\n\nUsage: agentgraph.exe [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>\n\nCommands:\n  index         Build or refresh the local index (incremental by content hash). Multi-root: `index --workspace <manifest.json>` or repeated `--workspace-root <dir>`\n  workspace     Workspace multi-root commands (single SQLite store + root_id)\n  stats         Show index statistics\n  find          Find symbol definitions by exact name (falls back to fuzzy on no match)\n  callers       List call sites / references of a symbol\n  blast-radius  High-level blast-radius recipe: auto sound vs default window + honesty payload\n  who-calls     High-level who-calls recipe: implementors separated by default; --noisy merges\n  impact        Blast radius: who transitively depends on this symbol\n  related       Files most related to a symbol (for retrieval scoping)\n  importers     Files that import a given file (module-level edges)\n  enrich        Optional LLM pass: one-lin